# WS3-03. Sources: spec/02-types.md §10 ("Every arithmetic and shift operation is
# defined"; count masked to the width) and spec/04 §5 (<< fills with zero). In C99
# 6.5.7p4 a left shift of a negative signed value, or one whose result does not fit,
# is undefined; the emitted C must avoid it (host UBSan line). Values: -1<<3 = -8,
# 1<<31 = -2147483648, 0x40000000<<1 = -2147483648, -2<<4 = -32.
profiles: host hosted-amiga hosted-amiga-13
expect: output
contrast: shl(-1, 3) ==> shl(1, 3)
contrast-expect: output
--- output
-8 -2147483648 -2147483648 -32
--- contrast-output
8 -2147483648 -2147483648 -32
